    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71669024\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p>“Test-drive the car before you put down a deposit,” my mother has always said. It sounds oddly progressive coming from someone of her generation, but she has long believed that living together before marriage is  sensible . If it does not work out, you go your separate ways. At least you’ve tried, she says, without the added complications of divorce, dividing property and untangling two lives legally. Of course, she also thinks it can be an easy escape for men who want the comforts of a relationship without committing all the way.</p><p>It is an argument that captures the peculiar place live-in relationships occupy in India: they are simultaneously a sensible experiment, depending on whom you ask, and a convenient arrangement that lets one partner indefinitely postpone the question of marriage.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 07, 2026 12:25 pm IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71669024\" data-title=\"Live-in relationships in India: Is marriage still the endgame?\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/columns/live-in-relationships-in-india-is-marriage-still-the-endgame/article71669024.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-fa7d358102b88e4f0a52e9ec-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/columns/live-in-relationships-in-india-is-marriage-still-the-endgame/article71669024.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                      