    "content_text": "“Test-drive the car before you put down a deposit,” my mother has always said. It sounds oddly progressive coming from someone of her generation, but she has long believed that living together before marriage is  sensible . If it does not work out, you go your separate ways. At least you’ve tried, she says, without the added complications of divorce, dividing property and untangling two lives legally. Of course, she also thinks it can be an easy escape for men who want the comforts of a relationship without committing all the way.\nIt is an argument that captures the peculiar place live-in relationships occupy in India: they are simultaneously a sensible experiment, depending on whom you ask, and a convenient arrangement that lets one partner indefinitely postpone the question of marriage.\nPublished\n- November 07, 2026 12:25 pm IST\nCopy link\nEmail\nFacebook\nTwitter\nTelegram\nLinkedIn\nWhatsApp\nReddit\nREAD LATER\nSEE ALL\nRemove\nRelated Topics",
